The problem was with my Nginx Docker setup/configuration: I am using
`nginx:alpine`
, which has the configuration files at
`/etc/nginx/conf.d/`
. There,
`default.conf`
 defines the default configuration of Nginx. So, I had to remove
`default.conf`
 and copy my configuration there instead. In the
`Dockerfile`
:

```
COPY nginx.conf /etc/nginx/conf.d/nginx.conf
RUN rm /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf
```

Of course, I also had to define the standard route in
`nginx.conf`
 then:

```
server {
    location / {
        root /usr/share/nginx/html;
    }

    location /health {
        return 200 'alive';
        add_header Content-Type text/plain;
    }
}
```

